    # Spanish (Spain). Machine translated, NOT reviewed by a native speaker - see the header
    # of Tlc.Localization.psm1. Safe for what it covers: field labels, buttons and hints.
    # Nothing that reaches a bundle is translated.
    #
    # Product names stay in English on purpose. "Teams admin center", "Teams Rooms" and
    # "PowerShell" are what the controls in those products actually say, so translating them
    # would send an engineer looking for something that does not exist under that name.
    #
    # THIS FILE MUST BE SAVED AS UTF-8 WITH A BOM. Measured on 2026-09-15: without one,
    # Import-PowerShellDataFile on Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads the bytes as the ANSI
    # codepage and every accent becomes mojibake - "Espanol" arrives as "EspaA+-ol" - while
    # PowerShell 7 reads it correctly either way. Tlc.Localization.Tests.ps1 asserts the BOM
    # for that reason, because the general rule elsewhere in this toolbox is the opposite.

